abstract: >-
  Alberto Research is a Python package for scientific research automation. It
  discovers literature through Crossref and Semantic Scholar, normalises and
  deduplicates DOIs, and resolves full texts through a pluggable resolver chain
  over legal open-access sources such as Unpaywall, OpenAlex, CORE, DOAJ and
  Europe PMC. Screening and deep reading are delegated to OpenClaw-backed LLM
  tasks whose structured output is persisted only after JSON Schema validation,
  and results feed digest and newsletter generation as well as Zotero and Notion
  synchronisation. All external content is treated as hostile input. Optional
  legacy resolvers targeting shadow libraries exist but are disabled by default
  and are the operator's sole legal responsibility.
